          "label": "FY2025",
          "start": "2025-01-01",
          "end": "2025-12-31"
        },
        "value": "33.10",
        "unit": "percent"
      }
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "COMPANY_05 shows modest total net revenue growth of 2.75% YoY, supported by both net interest income (+3.09%) and noninterest revenue (+2.39%). However, the 33.1% surge in credit loss provisions to $14.2 billion signals significant deterioration in credit quality, particularly in consumer (PRODUCT_26) and wholesale portfolios. The noninterest revenue growth occurred despite a $6.3 billion decline in Other income, mainly due to the absence of a $7.9 billion ENTITY_04 gain in 2024, partially offset by a $588 million ENTITY_05 gain in 2025. Market and credit risks noted in Item 1A remain elevated. Given the offsetting dynamics of revenue growth versus sharply rising credit costs, a HOLD recommendation is appropriate pending clarity on credit cycle trajectory."
